within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.M_MusculoSkeletalSystem.M01A_AntiinflammatoryAndAntirheumaticProductsNonStero.M01AE02_Naproxen;
model Naproxen_Bjrnsson2011_PD_pi
  "sigmoid_emax exposure-response sweep — Björnsson_2011 :: PI (pain intensity)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep(
    E0 = 52.7,      // [mm]
    Emax = -1,  // [mm]
    EC50 = 0.135,  // [mol/m3; mmol l -1 × 1]
    gamma = 1.61,
    exposure_per_s = 1);   // 1 mmol l -1 per second
  // inhibition_sign: effect_direction=inhibition with a positive Emax (Q320) — sign flipped
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 1.4, Interval = 0.0028),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Naproxen_Bjrnsson2011_PD_pi</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Björnsson MA et al., <i>British journal of clinical pharmacology 71(6):899–906</i> 2011 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-2125.2011.03924.x\">doi:10.1111/j.1365-2125.2011.03924.x</a>) — pain intensity [mm] against unbound naproxen mmol l -1 — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: sigmoid_emax.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =       52.7 mm       drug-free response (baseline) (PIbaseline, Q324)
  Emax  =          1 mm       maximal effect term (Emax, Q320)
  EC50  =      0.135 mmol l -1 exposure at half of the maximal effect term (EC50, Q321)
  gamma =       1.61          Hill coefficient (g, Q325)</pre><p>The algebra is <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep\">SigmoidEmaxSweep</a>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one mmol l -1 of unbound naproxen per second of simulated time (exposure is in mol/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 52.7   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (0.135 mmol l -1)  response 52.2
  exposure -> infinity  response 51.7</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Björnsson_2011: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Naproxen_Bjrnsson2011_PD_pi;
